# Liquid Glass

Following Apple's *Adopting Liquid Glass* and WWDC25 "Build a SwiftUI app with
the new design". Target is iOS 26+ with **no** legacy fallback path.

## Get it from the system first

`TabView` + `Tab`, `NavigationStack` toolbars, `.sheet`, `.alert`, `Menu`,
`List`/`Form` already render as Liquid Glass on iOS 26. Use them and add
nothing. Most screens in this kit contain zero glass code.

## When you write custom glass

Only for the **floating / navigation layer**: a floating action bar, a paywall
CTA, a compose button. `Core/DesignSystem/GlassActionBar.swift` is the kit's
implementation — reuse it rather than writing `.glassEffect` inline.

```swift
GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 12) {
    HStack(spacing: 12) {
        GlassCapsuleButton(title: "Upgrade") { }
        GlassCircleButton(systemImage: "plus", accessibilityLabel: "Add") { }
    }
}
```

- `.glassEffect(_:in:)` for custom shapes; `.buttonStyle(.glass)` /
  `.glassProminent` for buttons.
- `.interactive()` on the primary control.
- Group related shapes in one `GlassEffectContainer` so they blend and morph
  together. Two separate containers side by side is a bug.

## Never

- **Glass on content.** List rows, cards, form sections, sheets full of text —
  all opaque. Use `Color(.secondarySystemGroupedBackground)`.
- **Glass on glass.** Whatever sits behind a glass control must be solid, or the
  material samples itself and turns to mud.
- Hard opaque overlays that defeat Reduce Transparency or Increase Contrast.
- `UIDesignRequiresCompatibility` — we ship the new design, not the old look.
- iOS 17–25 `if #available` design branches.

## Colour and type

- One brand token: `AccentColor` in the asset catalog. Everything else is a
  semantic system colour so both appearances and accessibility settings work.
- System text styles only (`.headline`, `.subheadline`, …) — never a fixed
  point size for body copy. Dynamic Type must work.
- Spacing from `Theme.Spacing`, radii from `Theme.Radius`.
- Verify light **and** dark. The design system has no third mode.
